# Model artifacts are checksummed (SHA-256 in models/registry.json and the model_registry table):
# git must store and check them out byte-for-byte, never converting line endings. Before this,
# Windows checkouts (CRLF) and the repository (LF) differed and non-Windows clones failed the
# checksum, so the tyre endpoint refused to serve models (found by CI, Phase 8).
models/tires/** -text
*.npz binary
*.parquet binary
# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers (`bash -s < ops/db/restore_drill.sh`, CI): always LF, or bash
# fails on the carriage returns of a Windows checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
